<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15699" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτί-στομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speaking in good
			idiom,</i> or <i>with precision,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cor.</u>
				38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					6.150
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>with a good mouth</i> or <i>opening,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόλπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					5.4.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					17.1.6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. βέλεα</span>
			<i>evenly tipped,</i> i. e. <i>not sharp</i> or <i>jagged</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανταχόθεν ὁμαλά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					19
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VC</u>
				11
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ξὸΐς</span>
			<i>plain</i> chisel (not toothed), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.3073.148
			</span></i> (Lebad.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
